{
  "//": [
    "Machine-readable parity sets for docs/API.md. Regenerate in the same",
    "change as any route or IPC command you add.",
    "http.routes  <- crates/slipscan-server/src/routes.rs, the `app()` router",
    "ipc.commands <- apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/lib.rs, generate_handler![]",
    "client.calls <- apps/desktop/src/lib/api/client.ts, every call(\"name\")",
    "",
    "A route existing does not mean the operation is served: device_init,",
    "device_rotate, device_reset, device_forget and the three device_pair_*",
    "routes are registered so they can REFUSE and name the local command",
    "instead (they create or destroy key material, or need a human in front",
    "of the device). They are counted here as routes because the router has",
    "them; the working implementation of each is the IPC command.",
    "",
    "missing_from_client is empty, and CI keeps it that way: every registered",
    "IPC command has a client.ts wrapper. Wrappers are written when the command",
    "is, ahead of the screen that will call it (ROADMAP.md Phase 6.9), so the",
    "IPC layer is never the surface left waiting on a UI.",
    "",
    "DO NOT hand-edit the lists or counts below -- `npm run parity:sync`",
    "derives them from the three sources named above, and `npm run parity:check`",
    "fails CI when they drift. They were hand-maintained until 2026-08-03 and",
    "were wrong by three features when the check was finally written."
  ],
